<title>INDIA: Indian soybean down, soyoil up, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean down, soyoil up, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices decreased by 100-150 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Thursday on increased arrivals. Plant delivery rates stayed at previous levels. Business volume was good and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil refined was up by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand in local markets, but soyoil solvent was steady. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly down on poor export demand. Soymeal yellow was $265-268 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) west coast Indian ports. Rapeseed extraction was $95-97 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export and was 3,350-3,400 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
